{"module":"world","voice":"female","duration":232.7,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"A world system","start":0.0,"end":1.2,"words":[[0.06,0.23],[0.23,0.58],[0.58,1.11]]},{"el":"intro","text":"American racism was part of a global system of empire.","start":2.0,"end":5.77,"words":[[2.05,2.58],[2.58,3.12],[3.12,3.32],[3.32,3.52],[3.52,3.66],[3.66,3.79],[3.79,4.26],[4.26,4.67],[4.67,4.8],[4.8,5.27]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Seeing that system helps explain why the same patterns appear on every continent, and what other countries have tried in order to repair them.","start":6.12,"end":13.64,"words":[[6.17,6.5],[6.5,6.7],[6.7,7.1],[7.1,7.43],[7.43,7.97],[7.97,8.17],[8.17,8.3],[8.3,8.56],[8.56,8.96],[8.96,9.23],[9.23,9.36],[9.36,9.63],[9.63,10.29],[10.53,10.73],[10.73,10.93],[10.93,11.13],[11.13,11.59],[11.59,11.79],[11.79,12.12],[12.12,12.26],[12.26,12.46],[12.46,12.59],[12.59,12.92],[12.92,13.19]]},{"el":"h0","text":"Abolition paid the enslavers","start":13.99,"end":16.12,"words":[[14.03,14.69],[14.69,15.02],[15.02,15.18],[15.18,15.92]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Britain banned the slave trade in 1807 and slavery in most of its colonies in 1833.","start":16.82,"end":24.1,"words":[[16.89,17.38],[17.38,17.72],[17.72,17.88],[17.88,18.3],[18.3,18.71],[18.71,18.88],[18.88,19.87],[19.87,20.12],[20.12,20.79],[20.79,20.95],[20.95,21.37],[21.37,21.53],[21.53,21.78],[21.78,22.36],[22.36,22.53],[22.53,23.61]]},{"el":"s0","text":"It paid £20 million in compensation, about 40% of the government's annual budget, to slaveholders, not to the people they had enslaved.","start":24.45,"end":34.12,"words":[[24.51,24.64],[24.64,24.92],[24.92,25.68],[25.68,26.1],[26.1,26.24],[26.24,27.13],[27.38,27.72],[27.72,28.41],[28.41,28.55],[28.55,28.69],[28.69,29.38],[29.38,29.8],[29.8,30.28],[30.52,30.66],[30.66,31.56],[31.8,32.01],[32.01,32.15],[32.15,32.29],[32.29,32.63],[32.63,32.84],[32.84,33.05],[33.05,33.67]]},{"el":"s0","text":"The loan raised to pay it was not fully paid off until 2015.","start":34.47,"end":38.74,"words":[[34.52,34.66],[34.66,34.95],[34.95,35.32],[35.32,35.46],[35.46,35.68],[35.68,35.82],[35.82,36.04],[36.04,36.26],[36.26,36.55],[36.55,36.84],[36.84,36.99],[36.99,37.35],[37.35,38.29]]},{"el":"s0","text":"France forced Haiti to pay for its own freedom (see the module “Before race”).","start":39.09,"end":44.74,"words":[[39.11,39.59],[39.59,39.98],[39.98,40.47],[40.47,40.66],[40.66,40.95],[40.95,41.15],[41.15,41.44],[41.44,41.73],[41.73,42.31],[42.31,42.5],[42.5,42.7],[42.7,43.28],[43.28,43.67],[43.67,44.15]]},{"el":"h1","text":"The scramble for Africa","start":45.64,"end":47.39,"words":[[45.69,45.86],[45.86,46.55],[46.55,46.72],[46.72,47.23]]},{"el":"s1","text":"At the Berlin Conference (1884–85), European powers set rules for dividing Africa among themselves, with no Africans present.","start":48.09,"end":58.4,"words":[[48.14,48.3],[48.3,48.46],[48.46,48.88],[48.88,49.53],[49.53,51.34],[51.63,52.37],[52.37,52.78],[52.78,53.03],[53.03,53.36],[53.36,53.52],[53.52,54.18],[54.18,54.67],[54.67,55.0],[55.0,55.74],[56.03,56.28],[56.28,56.53],[56.53,57.18],[57.18,57.84]]},{"el":"s1","text":"In King Leopold II's Congo Free State, forced rubber collection brought mass killing, mutilation and famine; estimates of the dead range widely, from about 1 million to 10 million.","start":58.75,"end":71.47,"words":[[58.8,58.95],[58.95,59.18],[59.18,59.8],[59.8,60.42],[60.42,60.88],[60.88,61.12],[61.12,61.58],[61.85,62.16],[62.16,62.47],[62.47,63.09],[63.09,63.4],[63.4,63.63],[63.63,64.09],[64.36,65.22],[65.22,65.45],[65.45,65.91],[66.18,66.8],[66.8,66.96],[66.96,67.11],[67.11,67.34],[67.34,67.81],[67.81,68.35],[68.62,68.93],[68.93,69.32],[69.32,69.55],[69.55,70.01],[70.01,70.17],[70.17,70.4],[70.4,70.94]]},{"el":"s1","text":"In German South West Africa (Namibia), German troops killed tens of thousands of Herero and Nama people in 1904–08; Germany acknowledged it as genocide in 2021.","start":71.82,"end":84.7,"words":[[71.87,72.03],[72.03,72.49],[72.49,72.81],[72.81,73.12],[73.12,73.59],[73.59,74.21],[74.49,74.96],[74.96,75.35],[75.35,75.66],[75.66,75.97],[75.97,76.13],[76.13,76.76],[76.76,76.91],[76.91,77.38],[77.38,77.61],[77.61,77.93],[77.93,78.32],[78.32,78.47],[78.47,80.27],[80.55,81.09],[81.09,81.8],[81.8,81.95],[81.95,82.11],[82.11,82.81],[82.81,82.97],[82.97,84.22]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Hitler's American model","start":85.6,"end":87.19,"words":[[85.6,86.04],[86.04,86.63],[86.63,87.0]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Law professor James Q.","start":87.89,"end":89.86,"words":[[87.95,88.09],[88.09,88.6],[88.6,89.04],[89.04,89.33]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Whitman showed in 2017 that Nazi lawyers drafting the 1935 Nuremberg Laws studied American race law, including state bans on interracial marriage, Jim Crow, and race-based immigration and citizenship rules.","start":90.21,"end":107.15,"words":[[90.26,90.77],[90.77,91.11],[91.11,91.28],[91.28,92.46],[92.46,92.72],[92.72,93.14],[93.14,93.56],[93.56,94.16],[94.16,94.33],[94.33,95.6],[95.6,96.44],[96.44,96.7],[96.7,97.21],[97.21,97.88],[97.88,98.22],[98.22,98.48],[98.77,99.45],[99.45,99.87],[99.87,100.21],[100.21,100.38],[100.38,101.23],[101.23,101.82],[102.12,102.46],[102.46,102.88],[103.18,103.43],[103.43,104.2],[104.2,105.04],[105.04,105.3],[105.3,106.14],[106.14,106.57]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Some of them found U.S. law harsher than they were prepared to go, for example in its “one drop” definitions of race.","start":107.5,"end":114.07,"words":[[107.56,107.75],[107.75,107.89],[107.89,108.08],[108.08,108.41],[108.41,108.74],[109.06,109.2],[109.2,109.46],[109.46,109.65],[109.65,109.85],[109.85,109.98],[109.98,110.44],[110.44,110.57],[110.57,110.83],[111.06,111.19],[111.19,111.72],[111.72,111.85],[111.85,112.04],[112.04,112.24],[112.24,112.5],[112.5,113.16],[113.16,113.29],[113.29,113.62]]},{"el":"h3","text":"Apartheid, and the world's response","start":114.97,"end":118.13,"words":[[115.03,115.86],[116.23,116.54],[116.54,116.75],[116.75,117.27],[117.27,118.0]]},{"el":"s3","text":"South Africa's apartheid system (1948–1994) classified every person by race and confined Black South Africans to “homelands.”","start":118.83,"end":129.54,"words":[[118.88,119.21],[119.21,119.78],[119.78,120.35],[120.35,120.85],[120.85,123.47],[123.76,124.5],[124.5,124.83],[124.83,125.24],[125.24,125.48],[125.48,125.81],[125.81,126.06],[126.06,126.72],[126.72,127.04],[127.04,127.37],[127.37,128.03],[128.03,128.19],[128.19,129.01]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Police killed 69 protesters at Sharpeville in 1960.","start":129.89,"end":134.57,"words":[[129.93,130.33],[130.33,130.65],[130.65,131.44],[131.44,132.16],[132.16,132.32],[132.32,132.79],[132.79,132.95],[132.95,134.07]]},{"el":"s3","text":"A global divestment movement, led in the U.S. by students, churches and the Congressional Black Caucus, pushed Congress to pass sanctions in 1986 over President Reagan's veto.","start":134.92,"end":148.19,"words":[[134.97,135.12],[135.12,135.65],[135.65,136.48],[136.48,137.08],[137.34,137.57],[137.57,137.72],[137.72,137.87],[137.87,138.24],[138.62,138.85],[138.85,139.6],[139.86,140.39],[140.39,140.61],[140.61,140.76],[140.76,141.59],[141.59,141.89],[141.89,142.34],[142.61,142.91],[142.91,143.43],[143.43,143.58],[143.58,143.81],[143.81,144.41],[144.41,144.56],[144.56,145.69],[145.69,145.99],[145.99,146.67],[146.67,147.2],[147.2,147.65]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Nelson Mandela was freed in 1990 and elected president in 1994, and a Truth and Reconciliation Commission followed.","start":148.54,"end":158.1,"words":[[148.6,149.07],[149.07,149.61],[149.61,149.84],[149.84,150.15],[150.15,150.3],[150.3,151.3],[151.3,151.54],[151.54,152.08],[152.08,152.77],[152.77,152.93],[152.93,154.16],[154.43,154.66],[154.66,154.82],[154.82,155.13],[155.13,155.36],[155.36,156.51],[156.51,157.05],[157.05,157.6]]},{"el":"h4","text":"Other settler nations","start":159.0,"end":160.59,"words":[[159.05,159.32],[159.32,159.78],[159.78,160.42]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Australia's “White Australia” policy restricted non-European immigration from 1901 into the 1970s, and its governments removed Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander children from their families (the Stolen Generations); Prime Minister Kevin Rudd apologized in 2008.","start":161.29,"end":180.79,"words":[[161.34,162.09],[162.09,162.4],[162.4,163.08],[163.08,163.53],[163.53,164.29],[164.29,165.19],[165.19,165.95],[165.95,166.25],[166.25,167.16],[167.16,167.46],[167.46,167.61],[167.61,168.82],[169.09,169.31],[169.31,169.54],[169.54,170.3],[170.3,170.75],[170.75,171.58],[171.58,171.81],[171.81,172.19],[172.19,172.64],[172.64,173.17],[173.17,173.77],[173.77,174.08],[174.08,174.3],[174.3,174.83],[174.83,174.98],[174.98,175.51],[175.51,176.49],[176.76,177.14],[177.14,177.67],[177.67,178.04],[178.04,178.27],[178.27,179.1],[179.1,179.25],[179.25,180.24]]},{"el":"s4","text":"In Canada about 150,000 Indigenous children were sent to residential schools; the Truth and Reconciliation Commission called it cultural genocide in 2015, and Pope Francis apologized in 2022.","start":181.14,"end":196.14,"words":[[181.19,181.34],[181.34,181.78],[181.78,182.14],[182.14,183.9],[183.9,184.63],[184.63,185.22],[185.22,185.36],[185.36,185.65],[185.65,185.8],[185.8,186.53],[186.53,186.97],[187.23,187.37],[187.37,187.67],[187.67,187.88],[187.88,188.98],[188.98,189.49],[189.49,189.79],[189.79,189.93],[189.93,190.59],[190.59,191.25],[191.25,191.4],[191.4,192.35],[192.6,192.82],[192.82,193.11],[193.11,193.63],[193.63,194.43],[194.43,194.58],[194.58,195.67]]},{"el":"h5","text":"Can repair work?","start":197.04,"end":198.18,"words":[[197.04,197.22],[197.22,197.52],[197.52,197.76]]},{"el":"s5","text":"West Germany began paying reparations to Israel and Holocaust survivors in 1952.","start":198.88,"end":205.28,"words":[[198.94,199.25],[199.25,199.79],[199.79,200.17],[200.17,200.56],[200.56,201.4],[201.4,201.56],[201.56,202.02],[202.02,202.25],[202.25,202.87],[202.87,203.48],[203.48,203.64],[203.64,204.79]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Caribbean nations (CARICOM) adopted a ten-point reparations plan in 2013.","start":205.63,"end":210.92,"words":[[205.68,206.21],[206.21,206.68],[206.68,207.15],[207.39,207.86],[207.86,207.99],[207.99,208.53],[208.53,209.26],[209.26,209.53],[209.53,209.67],[209.67,210.47]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Germany pledged about €1.1 billion in development aid to Namibia in 2021, which many Herero and Nama leaders rejected as inadequate.","start":211.27,"end":221.06,"words":[[211.31,211.79],[211.79,212.2],[212.2,212.54],[212.54,213.76],[213.76,214.17],[214.17,214.31],[214.31,215.06],[215.06,215.26],[215.26,215.4],[215.4,215.87],[215.87,216.01],[216.01,217.1],[217.34,217.61],[217.61,217.88],[217.88,218.29],[218.29,218.5],[218.5,218.77],[218.77,219.11],[219.11,219.72],[219.72,219.86],[219.86,220.54]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Whether reparations, apologies and truth commissions repair harm, and in what form, is actively debated.","start":221.41,"end":228.99,"words":[[221.46,221.77],[221.77,222.71],[222.98,223.68],[223.68,223.91],[223.91,224.23],[224.23,224.85],[224.85,225.24],[225.24,225.55],[225.82,226.06],[226.06,226.21],[226.21,226.45],[226.45,226.76],[227.03,227.19],[227.19,227.73],[227.73,228.43]]},{"el":"s5","text":"The precedents themselves are documented.","start":229.34,"end":231.8,"words":[[229.39,229.51],[229.51,230.11],[230.11,230.59],[230.59,230.65],[230.65,231.37]]}]}